>2024</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11145482</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-ndt-3-211"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cummings</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Behavioral and neuropsychiatric outcomes in Alzheimer&#x02019;s disease</article-title><source>CNS Spectr</source><volume>10</volume><issue>Suppl 18</issue><fpage>22</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16273027</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-ndt-3-211"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Darreh-Shori</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Almkvist</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Guan</surname><given-names>ZZ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Sustained cholinesterase inhibition in AD patients receiving rivastigmine for 12 months</article-title><source>Neurology</source><volume>594</volume><fpage>563</fpage><lpage>72</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12196650</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13-ndt-3-211"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Darreh-Shori</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Hellstrom-Lindahl</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Flores-Flores</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Long-lasting acetylcholinesterase splice variations in anticholinesterase-treated Alzheimer&#x02019;s disease patients</article-title><source>J Neurochem</source><volume>885</volume><fpage>1102</fpage><lpage>13</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15009666</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14-ndt-3-211"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Darvesh</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hopkins